-- title:
--   Projective Weierstrass chart base change is a pullback
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $R$, $K$ a commutative ring equipped with an $R$-algebra structure, and $i \in \{0,1\}$. Write $\mathcal{A}$ for the graded ring $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,3, R)$ modulo the ideal generated by the homogeneous cubic $W.\mathrm{toProjective}.\mathrm{polynomial}$, graded in degree $n$ by the image of the $n$-th homogeneous submodule under the quotient map (the project notion `projModelGradingCR`), and similarly $\mathcal{B}$ for the corresponding graded quotient attached to the base-changed curve $W.\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ K)$ over $K$. The statement first introduces the graded ring homomorphism $\psi : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ induced on quotients by coefficientwise application of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ K$ to polynomials (legitimate because the image of the ideal generated by $W$'s projective polynomial is the ideal generated by that of the base-changed curve), which maps each graded piece into the corresponding one. Let $t$ denote the class of the variable $X_{![1,2]i}$, i.e. the second coordinate $Y$ when $i=0$ and the third coordinate $Z$ when $i=1$. The conclusion asserts that the square of affine schemes formed by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the map $\mathrm{Away.map}\ \psi\ t$ on degree-zero homogeneous localisations away from $t$, by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the two structure maps $K \to \mathcal{B}_0 \to \mathrm{Away}_{\psi(t)}(\mathcal{B})$ and $R \to \mathcal{A}_0 \to \mathrm{Away}_t(\mathcal{A})$, and by $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\ R\ K$, is a pullback square: the chart of the base-changed projective model is the fibre product of the chart over $R$ with $\mathrm{Spec}\,K$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$.
--
--   This records the compatibility of the two non-vanishing-coordinate charts $D_+(Y)$ and $D_+(Z)$ of the projective Weierstrass model with base change along $R \to K$, the affine-local form of the statement that the projective model of a Weierstrass curve commutes with base change. It is used to assemble the global base-change isomorphism of projective Weierstrass models, [`WeierstrassProjModel.kw_bc_baseChangeIso`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.kw_bc_baseChangeIso).
-- source:
